# Pick ONE of the providers below, copy this file to `.env`, and fill in the key.
# Then load: `set -a && . ./.env && set +a`
#
# Resolution priority is env > YAML > default. The grader injects MODEL_API_URL /
# MODEL_API_KEY / MODEL_NAME at evaluation time, so the same code runs unchanged.

# --- Option A: OpenRouter (RECOMMENDED — exact eval model) -----------------
# Hosts qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b — the same checkpoint the official grader uses.
# Sign up: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# MODEL_API_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# MODEL_NAME=qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b
#
# Optional but recommended: pin OpenRouter to a single backend so cross-provider
# routing (different quantization, different inference engine) does not add
# variance to local benchmarks. Alibaba is the model maker's own deployment,
# closest to the eval-time setup. Combine with a fixed seed for determinism.
# MODEL_PROVIDER_ONLY=alibaba
# MODEL_SEED=42

# --- Option B: Alibaba DashScope (international) ---------------------------
# Official Qwen provider. Confirm exact 3.5-35b-a3b availability in their catalog.
# Sign up: https://bailian.console.alibabacloud.com/
# Model catalog: https://help.aliyun.com/zh/model-studio/getting-started/models
# MODEL_API_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=sk-...
# MODEL_NAME=qwen3.5-35b-a3b

# --- Option C: DeepSeek V3 (cheap proxy, NOT a Qwen) ------------------------
# Useful for fast iteration (~$0.5 / 50-task run). Behavior differs from eval.
# MODEL_API_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1
# MODEL_API_KEY=sk-...
# MODEL_NAME=deepseek-chat
